On jade-flowered mat, golden-threaded screen unfurls,
Dawn moon pities zither strings, spring wind recalls mirror stand.
Zither strings kissed by dawn breeze, moon hangs low;
Fragrant trees shed blooms — day and dusk cease.
Husband’s return unknown, no word from blade’s edge;
I break branches, wipe tears, sit lost in longing.
